cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you implement, extend, or critique this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "Seam Specification"
abstract: >-
  A specification for observable agent-simulation interfaces. Defines a declarative
  manifest as the single source of truth for a simulation's surface, with two projections
  (human bindings and agent tool signatures) and an append-only crossing trace. Four
  affordances — trigger, dial, ratchet, gauge — are derived mechanically from three
  declared facts: writeability, domain shape, and liveness.
